    <info>
        <meta name="maintainer" content="daria.vladykina@suse.com" its:translate="no"/>
        <title>Preparing the hardware platform</title>
        <abstract>
            <para>Real-time applications require a hardware foundation configured for 
                minimal latency. This section describes how to configure server BIOS 
                and firmware settings. These adjustments eliminate low-level platform interference 
                before you begin latency testing.
            </para>
        </abstract>
    </info>
        <para>
            Before you start measuring hardware or operating system latencies, you must 
            optimize your machine settings:
        </para>
        <procedure xml:id="pro-firmware-prep">
            <title>Optimizing server firmware settings</title>
            <step>
                <para>
                    Access your server BIOS or firmware settings.
                </para>
            </step>
            <step>
                <para>
                    Set the machine for real-time performance. Note that these settings are vendor-specific.
                </para>
            </step>
            <step>
                <para>
                    Set everything to the lowest possible latency.
                </para>
            </step>
            <step>
                <para>
                    Turn down memory scrubbing to as little as possible.
                </para>
            </step>
        </procedure>
    
</topic>